  "root_cause": {
    "hypothesis": "The shared-memory tile is declared `__shared__ float tile[32][32]`, so the column read `tile[threadIdx.x][threadIdx.y]` has a row stride equal to the LDS bank count (32), aliasing every column element into a single bank and forcing 32-way serialization per wave.",
    "mechanism": "Row stride is 32 floats = 32 banks \u00d7 4B, so element (r, c) lives in bank ((r*32 + c) mod 32) = c. During the store phase threads within a wave share threadIdx.y (fixed c) and sweep threadIdx.x (varying r), so all 32 reads land in the same bank and serialize. On BW151 waves are 64-wide against a 32-bank LDS (already two half-wave cycles), so this 32-way conflict compounds and inflates ELAPSED_MS to 1.2\u20131.5 ms instead of ~0.5 ms. Correctness is unaffected because the indexing math is right \u2014 only throughput suffers.",
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "bug_type": "bank_conflict",
    "affected_lines": [
      36,
      45
    ]
  },
  "patch_plan": {
    "summary": "Pad the inner dimension of the shared tile from 32 to 33 to break the modulo-32 bank alias.",
    "diff": "@@\n-    __shared__ float tile[TILE][TILE];\n+    __shared__ float tile[TILE][TILE + 1];\n",
    "risks": [
      "Adds 32*4B = 128B of LDS per block (negligible vs. 64KB LDS budget).",
      "None to correctness; indexing is unchanged."
    ],
    "expected_effect": "STATUS: PASS remains, ELAPSED_MS drops ~2-3\u00d7 (into the ~0.4\u20130.6 ms range on 2048\u00d72048).",
    "validation_steps": [
      "hipcc -O2 -std=c++17 transpose_bank_conflict.hip -o transpose",
      "./transpose",
      "check STATUS: PASS and ELAPSED_MS significantly lower than baseline"
    ]
  },
